    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required the owner API to return `selfLink = \"/api/owners/\" + id`. The acceptance test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and then reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, asserting `$.selfLink`.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated by MapStruct, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (which generates the field, getter, and setter on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that derives it from the entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getId() == null ? null : \\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause both the GET responder (`RespondWithOwner`) and the POST responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) go through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, `selfLink` now appears consistently on every owner response. No OfficeFloor wiring changes were needed.",
